Javis Felagund <javisfelagund@yahoo.com.mx> deserves a cookie for saying:
> Hi again!

> sourcediving a little, a found this in uhitm.c:

> if function damageum(mdef, mattk), there are a lot of cases of the
> attacks you may inflict to a monster. The case for AD_CURS is also
> there. As I understand it, this is an attack for cursing another one's
> items,

No, this is a gremlin's intrinsic-removing attack.  Item-cursing is
generally the result of an AD_SPEL attack.  

> or something like that (in fact, it seems to cancel the monster,
> reading the code).

An AD_CURS attack against the player, when it's successful, removes a
random intrinsic.  Monster intrinsics, though, don't work the same way
as player intrinsics and are thus not as easy, code-wise, to remove.  I
don't even know if it can be done with monster data structured the way
it currently is.  

So, instead of dealing with intrinsic-stealing the same way it happens
when a player gets hit, the monster gets cancelled instead.

> But my problem comes when I see that this one only applies at night...
> so... ?does this means that I can only use this attack (being a
> gremlin maybe) at night?...

Correct.

> Of course, a gremlin can only attack any other monster with this
> attack at night, but, what about other monster that also can?

Theoretically, a non-gremlin monster with an AD_CURS attack could remove
intrinsics during the daytime.  I say theoretically because such a
monster does not exist.  

> In mhitm, the cases don't exclude that possibility and only gremlins
> at night may do that, but doesn't tells that any other monster with
> the attack could do it at any other time of the day/night...

mhitu.c and mhitm.c are essentially the same here.  When an AD_CURS
attack hits, the code checks:
  if (!night() && (pa == &mons[PM_GREMLIN])) break;
So if it's not night and the attacker is a gremlin, we jump out of this
case.  Otherwise, we proceed as usual.  This tells you that any monster
besides a gremlin has a chance of succeeding at any time of the day or
night.

> so, if i'm polymorphed in a gremlin, the restriction in uhitm is
> logical, but if i'm polyed in any other?...

You can't poly into a non-gremlin and have an AD_CURS attack as things
currently stand.  If we hypothesize such a monster, though, then yes,
you would be able to remove instrinsics (or cancel a monster, rather) at
any time of the day or night.

